events.content:
`onUpdate?: (value) => void` — clean API. Now write the code.

Files:

**src/line-chart.css** — theme-scoped tokens + component styles.

**src/LineChart.tsx** — the chart.

**src/App.tsx** — demo shell with theme toggle.

Let me write LineChart.tsx carefully.

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import './line-chart.css';

export interface LineSeries {
  name: string;
  values: number[];
}

interface LineChartProps {
  title: string;
  subtitle?: string;
  labels: string[];           // x categories
  series: LineSeries[];       // 1..4
  unit?: string;              // e.g. "тыс."
  formatValue?: (v: number) => string;
}
```

Layout:
```
const W = 760, H = 296;
const M = { top: 20, right: 136, bottom: 36, left: 44 };
plotW = W - M.left - M.right; plotH = H - M.top - M.bottom;
```

niceCeil: given max value → ticks. Implement: rawStep = max/4; magnitude = 10^floor(log10(rawStep)); normalized = rawStep/mag; step = (normalized<1.5?1: normalized<3?2: normalized<7?5:10)*mag; niceMax = ceil(max/step)*step; ticks 0..niceMax.

x(i) = M.left + (plotW) * (i/(n-1)).
y(v) = M.top + plotH * (1 - v/niceMax).

Series color: `var(--lc-series-${idx+1})` — via CSS classes `.lc-series-1 { stroke: var(--lc-series-1); fill: ... }`? For lines stroke only; dots fill + surface ring stroke. Classes: `lc-line lc-line--1` etc. Use CSS:

```css
.lc-line { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
.lc-line--1 { stroke: var(--lc-series-1); }
.lc-dot--1 { fill: var(--lc-series-1); }
```

Simpler: inline style={{ stroke: `var(--lc-series-${i+1})` }} — dynamic but fine in React. I'll use inline styles for series colors (fewer CSS permutations, still CSS-var-driven so theme-flip is automatic).

End labels collision: compute yEnd for each series; sort desc by value; threshold 20px between adjacent label centers; if violation → hide all end labels (legend + tooltip carry identity). Actually maybe hide only colliding ones? Skill: "fall back to the legend + tooltip" — I'll drop labels for the colliding pair but keep non-colliding? Consistency argues all-or-none. I'll do all-or-none.

End dot: r=4.5, fill series, stroke var(--lc-surface) strokeWidth 2 → 9px dot + 2px ring.

Crosshair: when activeIndex != null:
